---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Contact Us - Finsiva" description="Contact Finsiva for inquiries, feedback, or suggestions about our tax calculators and platform.">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <main class="min-h-screen">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-8 dark:text-on-primary">Contact Us: We're Here to Help You Navigate Your Financial Journey</h1>

        <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224154-26032ffc0d07?w=1200&q=80" alt="Modern office contact desk" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />

        <div class="prose max-w-none space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted">
          <p>Welcome to the Finsiva contact page. We know that arriving here might mean you're feeling a little overwhelmed—perhaps you're staring at a spreadsheet filled with numbers that just don't seem to add up, or maybe you're trying to figure out how a sudden, unexpected change in your life impacts your tax bracket. We want you to know, first and foremost, that we get it. Taxes and personal finance aren't just about math; they're about your life, your hard work, your family's security, and your future. That's exactly why we are here, and that's why this page exists.</p>

          <p>Our foundational mission at Finsiva has always been to transform the cold, confusing, and often intimidating world of tax regulations into clear, actionable, and profoundly human-centered guidance. We deeply believe that everyone deserves to understand their financial standing without needing an advanced degree in accounting or having to pay exorbitant fees to professional advisors just to get a basic answer. Whether you're a recent college graduate filing your tax return for the very first time, a seasoned freelancer juggling multiple complex income streams, a dedicated small business owner trying to make payroll, or a retiree navigating pension tax rules, your unique financial journey matters to us.</p>

          <p>We've designed our tools to be as intuitive as possible, but we also recognize that software can only go so far. Sometimes, you just need to connect with a real human being to report an issue, suggest a brilliant new feature, or ask a clarifying question about how a specific calculation was performed. We don't hide behind automated chatbots or endless phone trees. When you reach out to Finsiva, you are reaching a dedicated team of developers, researchers, and financial enthusiasts who genuinely care about making your life easier.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Real Stories, Real Support: When to Reach Out</h2>
          <p>To give you a better idea of how we can assist you, and to illustrate the kinds of conversations we love having with our users, here are a few detailed scenarios where reaching out to our team might be exactly what you need:</p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mt-6 mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">Scenario 1: The Freelancer's Dilemma with Quarterly Estimated Taxes</h3>
          <p>Imagine you're Sarah, a talented graphic designer who recently made the brave leap from a traditional, comfortable 9-to-5 corporate job to full-time freelancing. In her first year, business booms—she lands more clients than she ever anticipated. But as the first quarter draws to a close, a deep panic sets in. She has no idea how much she needs to set aside for self-employment taxes, nor does she know if her home office deduction, internet bills, and equipment depreciation apply to her current setup. She uses the Finsiva calculator but feels unsure about which specific deductions she legally qualifies for in her state.</p>
          <p>If you find yourself in Sarah's shoes, drop us a line! While we must emphasize that we do not provide official legal or tax advice, we can absolutely guide you on how to best utilize our tools. We can show you how to simulate different income scenarios, how to toggle specific self-employment settings in our interface, and direct you to our most relevant educational articles. We want to help you feel entirely prepared rather than panicked when tax day inevitably arrives.</p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mt-6 mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">Scenario 2: The Expat's Cross-Border Confusion</h3>
          <p>Or consider David, a senior software engineer who just accepted his absolute dream job in Berlin, Germany, but remains a citizen of the United States. Suddenly, he is thrust into a chaotic labyrinth of foreign earned income exclusions, foreign tax credits, and dual-filing requirements. It's a highly stressful transition, and standard, run-of-the-mill tax calculators simply don't cut it—they don't account for international tax treaties or the nuances of living abroad.</p>
          <p>If you are experiencing an international move and are confused by how our platform calculates dual-jurisdiction scenarios, please reach out. Our specialized support team can explain the underlying logic behind our international tax algorithms. We can help you understand exactly how your estimated net income was derived across borders, point you toward the correct input fields for foreign credits, and ensure you are maximizing the utility of our global calculators.</p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mt-6 mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">Scenario 3: The Small Business Owner Scaling Up</h3>
          <p>Then there's Elena, who runs a beloved local boutique bakery. After years of doing everything herself, she is finally ready to hire her first two full-time employees. She is thrilled about the growth, but absolutely terrified of payroll taxes, employer contributions, workers' compensation nuances, and general compliance. When she tries to forecast her new, increased labor costs on Finsiva, she gets stuck trying to decipher the employer versus employee tax split.</p>
          <p>We absolutely love helping users like Elena! A quick email to our support team can help clarify which toggle switches and advanced settings in our calculator accurately represent the specific payroll tax burdens in her state or country. We can help her model out the true cost of her new hires, giving her the confidence she needs to sign those employment contracts.</p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mt-6 mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">Scenario 4: The Crypto Investor Navigating New Regulations</h3>
          <p>Finally, consider Marcus, who started investing in cryptocurrency a few years ago. With recent changes in tax regulations regarding digital assets, staking rewards, and capital gains, Marcus is entirely lost. He doesn't know how to classify his different types of crypto income on our calculators.</p>
          <p>When Marcus contacts us, we can direct him to our newly updated crypto-tax modules and explain how our system differentiates between short-term capital gains, long-term investments, and standard income generated from staking. Your feedback on emerging financial trends like crypto helps us build better tools for everyone, so never hesitate to ask!</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">How to Get in Touch with the Finsiva Team</h2>
          <p>We offer several tailored communication channels depending on the specific nature of your request. By routing your message to the correct inbox, you help us ensure that the most qualified team member assists you as quickly as possible. We aim to respond to all messages within two business days. However, please be aware that response times may vary during peak tax seasons (typically March through April in North America, and October for extended deadlines) or directly following major platform updates.</p>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface mt-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">General Inquiries, Feature Requests & Feedback</h3>
            <p class="text-body dark:text-muted"><a href="mailto:ornacasa11@gmail.com" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">ornacasa11@gmail.com</a></p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted">Use this address for general questions, feature requests, or broad feedback about your experience. We are always, always eager to hear how we can improve. If you have a brilliant idea for a new calculator, a suggestion for a user interface tweak, or a feature that would simply make your financial planning life easier, we want to hear all about it. When you email us, please include your country and the specific type of tax scenario you are interested in, so we can route your message to the right regional specialist. We faithfully respond to all emails within two business days during our normal operations.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface mt-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">Technical Support & Bug Reporting</h3>
            <p class="text-body dark:text-muted">support@finsiva.com</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted">For technical issues with our calculators, broken website links, accessibility problems, or account-related inquiries, please use our dedicated support address. Our engineering team actively monitors this inbox throughout the day and rigorously prioritizes any bugs that affect calculation accuracy or core site functionality. If you happen to notice a discrepancy between our generated results and official tax authority figures, please include both values, the specific jurisdiction, and a screenshot if possible. This allows our developers to investigate promptly, replicate the issue, and push a fix to our live site.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface mt-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">Press, Media & Analyst Inquiries</h3>
            <p class="text-body dark:text-muted">media@finsiva.com</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted">Journalists, financial bloggers, podcast hosts, and industry analysts covering personal finance, tax technology, or regulatory compliance are always welcome to request data, interviews, or background information from our leadership team. We are happy to provide aggregate (and strictly anonymized) usage statistics, insightful commentary on recent tax policy changes, and high-resolution screenshots or brand assets for publication. We kindly ask that media inquiries include your publication's name, your working deadline, and a brief description of the story angle so we can prepare the most relevant and helpful information for you.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface mt-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">Connect with Us on Social Media</h3>
            <p class="text-body dark:text-muted">Engage with us online! We regularly post updates on new calculators, bite-sized tax tips, and easy-to-understand summaries of complex policy changes.</p>
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted list-disc pl-5">
              <li><a href="https://twitter.com/finsiva" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">Twitter / X</a> — Join the vibrant conversation for real-time announcements, quick financial tips, and rapid-fire updates during the busiest parts of tax season.</li>
              <li><a href="https://linkedin.com/company/finsiva" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">LinkedIn</a> — Connect with us for professional updates, company news, open job roles, and deep, analytical dives into the intersection of finance and technology.</li>
              <li><a href="https://youtube.com/@finsiva" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">YouTube</a> — Watch our highly detailed video guides and step-by-step calculator walkthroughs designed specifically to make complex topics visually simple and easy to digest.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-10 mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Partnerships and Strategic Collaborations</h2>
          <p>At Finsiva, we firmly believe that improving global financial literacy is a massive team effort that cannot be achieved in a silo. If you are representing an organization interested in partnering with us, or if you have a unique business proposal, we would be absolutely thrilled to hear from you. We actively seek out and foster collaborations with financial educators, reputable accounting firms, non-profit organizations, government agencies, and complementary technology platforms that share our core mission: making tax and financial information universally accessible, radically transparent, and remarkably easy to understand.</p>
          <p>When submitting a partnership proposal to our team, please take a moment to comprehensively describe your organization, the specific nature of the proposed collaboration, and your expected timeline for the project. Our business development team reviews all partnership proposals within five business days and will promptly follow up to schedule an exploratory discovery call if there appears to be a strong mutual fit. We are especially, deeply passionate about supporting initiatives that expand financial access to historically underserved regions, programs that improve foundational financial literacy for high school students and young adults, or technical collaborations that integrate our seamless tax education directly into existing payroll, HR, and freelance management platforms.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-12 mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Send Us a Message Directly</h2>
          <p>Sometimes, the absolute easiest and fastest way to reach out is right here on this page. Please use the secure, encrypted form below to send a message directly to our central support desk. Whether you are reporting a minor visual glitch, passionately requesting a new country to be added to our global database, or simply want to tell us a heartwarming story about how our tool helped you budget enough money to put a down payment on your first home, we promise you this: we read every single submission. Your messages are what keep us motivated to build the best financial tools on the internet.</p>

          <form action="https://formspree.io/f/xpqvelrz" method="POST" class="space-y-4 mt-6">
            <div>
              <label for="contact-name" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1 dark:text-on-primary">Name</label>
              <input type="text" id="contact-name" name="name" required class="w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas px-4 py-2 text-ink focus:border-primary focus:outline-none dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface dark:text-on-primary" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="contact-email" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1 dark:text-on-primary">Email</label>
              <input type="email" id="contact-email" name="email" required class="w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas px-4 py-2 text-ink focus:border-primary focus:outline-none dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface dark:text-on-primary" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="contact-subject" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1 dark:text-on-primary">Subject</label>
              <input type="text" id="contact-subject" name="subject" required class="w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas px-4 py-2 text-ink focus:border-primary focus:outline-none dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface dark:text-on-primary" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="contact-message" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1 dark:text-on-primary">Message</label>
              <textarea id="contact-message" name="message" rows="4" required class="w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas px-4 py-2 text-ink focus:border-primary focus:outline-none dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface dark:text-on-primary"></textarea>
            </div>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary mt-4 py-2 px-6 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors">Send Message</button>
          </form>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-16 mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Exhaustive Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
          <p>Before you hit that send button, you might find that your burning question has already been answered! We've meticulously compiled an exhaustive list of the most common questions our users ask us on a daily basis. Take a look below to see if you can find an immediate, detailed solution to your query without having to wait for an email reply.</p>

          <div class="space-y-8 mt-8">
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">1. Do you provide official, legally binding tax or financial advice?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">No, we emphatically do not. Finsiva is exclusively an educational tool designed to help you estimate your taxes, model different scenarios, and better understand your overall financial situation. The calculations, articles, and information provided anywhere on our site should never, under any circumstances, be construed as professional financial, legal, or tax advice. We strongly and universally recommend consulting with a certified public accountant (CPA), an enrolled agent, or a qualified tax professional in your jurisdiction before making any major financial decisions, finalizing business structures, or filing your official tax returns.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">2. I found a discrepancy between your calculator's result and my actual tax bill. What should I do?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Tax laws are incredibly complex, constantly evolving, and highly localized. While our dedicated research team works tirelessly to keep our data models up to date, minor discrepancies can occasionally occur. This is usually due to highly specific local county taxes, unique personal deductions you may qualify for, or brand-new legislative changes that haven't yet been fully integrated into our algorithm. If you spot a significant error, please email <a href="mailto:support@finsiva.com" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">support@finsiva.com</a> with the detailed specifics (your exact location, the precise inputs you used, and the expected versus actual result). We rely heavily on our vigilant user community to help us maintain the absolute highest standard of accuracy!</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">3. Can I request a brand-new calculator for my specific country, state, or region?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Absolutely, yes! We are constantly and aggressively expanding our database to include more countries, states, provinces, and territories. If your specific jurisdiction isn't currently supported by our platform, please send us a passionate message using the form above or email us directly at <a href="mailto:ornacasa11@gmail.com" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">ornacasa11@gmail.com</a>. We heavily prioritize new geographical additions based directly on user demand, so every single request counts as a vote toward your country being added next.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">4. Is my highly sensitive financial data actually safe when I use your calculators?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Yes, completely. Your privacy and digital security are our paramount priorities. Finsiva's calculators operate almost entirely within your web browser (client-side). This architecture means that the salary figures, personal deductions, and private financial scenarios you input are never transmitted back to our central servers, they are never stored in our databases, and they are never, ever shared with third-party advertisers. Once you close your browser tab, your temporary session data vanishes. For more extensive details on our security practices, please review our comprehensive Privacy Policy linked below.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">5. Why haven't I received a response to my email inquiry yet?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">We sincerely do our very best to reply to all inquiries within two standard business days. If it has been longer than that, we ask that you first please check your spam, junk, or promotions folder, as our replies occasionally get filtered out by overzealous corporate email providers. Additionally, please understand that during peak tax seasons (such as March and April in the US and UK, or the End of Financial Year in Australia), our inbound response volume spikes dramatically, which may inevitably cause slight delays. Please feel free to send a gentle follow-up email if you haven't heard back within a full calendar week!</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">6. How can I, as an expert or developer, actively contribute to Finsiva?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">We absolutely love working with guest writers, seasoned tax experts, and talented software developers! If you have deep expertise in a specific area of taxation and would like to write a guest educational article for our blog, or if you're a skilled developer interested in contributing code to our open-source tools, please reach out via our general partnership email. We are always actively looking for passionate individuals to join our crusade to demystify complex finance for the masses.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">7. Do you offer a commercial API for your proprietary tax calculation engine?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Currently, our powerful tax API is strictly in a closed beta phase, available only for a few select enterprise partners. We deeply understand that many independent developers, startups, and established businesses would love to integrate our robust calculation engine seamlessly into their own applications, payroll systems, and HR platforms. If you are interested in joining the exclusive waitlist for our eventual public API release, please contact us with extensive details about your proposed use case, your projected monthly request volume, and your specific technical integration requirements.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">8. I have a suggestion for a feature that isn't a calculator. Do you still want to hear it?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">We most certainly do! While our core focus is undoubtedly on building the best tax calculators, we are always looking to improve the holistic user experience. Whether you want a new dashboard layout, a better way to export your calculation results to PDF or CSV, a dark mode toggle enhancement, or a completely new type of financial planning tool like a retirement forecaster, your ideas are the fuel that drives our product roadmap. Send them our way!</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">9. Are your services completely free to use?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">Yes! The vast majority of our consumer-facing calculators, educational blog articles, and knowledge center resources are 100% free for anyone to use. Our core mission is financial accessibility, and putting a paywall in front of basic tax knowledge goes directly against that ethos. We support our operations through unobtrusive, relevant advertising, select affiliate partnerships with trusted financial services, and our premium enterprise API offerings.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-ink dark:text-on-primary">10. Can I hire someone from Finsiva to do my personal taxes?</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body dark:text-muted">While we are immensely flattered by the trust you place in us, Finsiva is purely a software and educational technology company, not a certified public accounting firm. We do not have CPAs on staff available for hire to prepare, review, or file individual or corporate tax returns. However, we highly recommend using local professional directories or trusted online services to find a certified professional who perfectly suits your specific needs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-16 mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Quick Navigation Links</h2>
          <p>Still looking for more information, or just want to keep exploring? Navigate our site easily using these quick links to find exactly what you need to master your financial destiny.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-3 mt-6 list-disc pl-5">
            <li><a href="/countries/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">Browse Country Tax Information</a> — View comprehensive, meticulously updated tax rates, brackets, and rules for dozens of jurisdictions worldwide.</li>
            <li><a href="/blogs/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">Read Tax Blog Articles</a> — Dive deep into our expertly written, easy-to-read articles covering everything from basic budgeting principles to advanced corporate tax strategies.</li>
            <li><a href="/about/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">Learn About Finsiva</a> — Discover the unique origin story behind our company, meet our passionate team members, and read all about our core mission and values.</li>
            <li><a href="/knowledge/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">Tax Knowledge Center</a> — Access our extensive, plain-English glossary of financial terms and detailed explanations of notoriously complex tax concepts.</li>
            <li><a href="/privacy/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">Privacy Policy</a> — Read a transparent breakdown of exactly how we protect your personal data and why we prioritize your digital security above all else.</li>
            <li><a href="/terms/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link font-medium">Terms of Service</a> — Review the legal rules, user agreements, and general guidelines for utilizing the Finsiva platform and its associated suite of tools.</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-12 text-lg italic text-ink dark:text-on-primary font-medium text-center border-t border-hairline pt-8">Thank you so much for choosing Finsiva as your trusted financial companion. We eagerly look forward to hearing from you and helping you make the absolute most of your financial future!</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>